      ],
      "source": "https://www.nutleyhistoricalsociety.org/"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Painter Frank Fowler established an artists' colony on The Enclosure in the late 1880s, near the Third River that flows through Nutley's parks.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nutley%2C_New_Jersey"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Until 1966, the Newark Branch of the Erie‑Lackawanna Railroad served Nutley with stations at Walnut, Highfield, and Franklin Avenue.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nutley%2C_New_Jersey"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Nutley was incorporated as Franklin Township on February 18, 1874, carved out of Belleville Township.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nutley%2C_New_Jersey"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Kingsland Manor, a national historic place, sits on Nutley's northern edge and is one of the township's three owned historic sites.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11,
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
